Derive the declared route mode from the call, not from which context dialled.

Applies to /etc/asterisk/extensions_fanum.conf on the PBX, applied live with
`dialplan reload` (no restart).

  before: 762dea271e18505315c893a610802c69ef3b480679340ce2199d829030097438
  after:  d24bae7a69b6ecfea982608fcd23a3e90b5c708dfa57a2630fa616956efaac13

This is the defect that stopped every AI call after the cutover.

The gate compares the route mode the dialplan declares against the call_mode in
the HMAC-signed registry row, and refuses the dial when they disagree. The
reviewed design gives each mode its own outbound context -- [fanum-outbound]
declares `human`, [fanum-ai-outbound] declares `ai` -- and the file says so
outright: "Normal CRM calls continue to use [fanum-outbound]."

The CRM has only ever dialled through the tenant's one configured context. For
an AI call it switches the *answered* context to fanum-ai-bridge and leaves the
outbound context alone. So every AI call went out through [fanum-outbound],
declared itself `human`, contradicted its own registry row, was refused
authorization, and hung up with cause 21 before dialling. Before the cutover
there was no gate, so the mismatch had nothing to contradict and calls worked.

Deriving the mode from the inherited __FANUM_CALL_MODE the CRM already sets
makes the declaration describe the call that is actually being placed. Authority
does not move: the coordinator still checks the declared mode against the signed
durable row, so a forged or absent mode still fails closed, and an uncorrelated
call still falls through to the preserved legacy path.

The permanent fix belongs in fanum_dialplan_transform.py, which generates this
file and hard-codes the mode per context; until that is re-staged, a cutover
re-run regenerates the broken form. See docs/pbx-live-divergence.md.

--- a/extensions_fanum.conf
+++ b/extensions_fanum.conf
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 [fanum-outbound]
 exten => _X.,1,NoOp(Fanum SIP outbound: ${EXTEN})
  same => n,Set(FANUM_DIAL_TARGET=PJSIP/${EXTEN}@fanum-provider)
- same => n,Set(FANUM_ROUTE_MODE=human)
+ same => n,Set(FANUM_ROUTE_MODE=${IF($["${FANUM_CALL_MODE}"="ai"]?ai:human)})
  same => n,Goto(fanum-observed-place-call,${EXTEN},1)
  same => n,Hangup()
